From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:40:21 +0900
Subject: Screencast: finish the GPU's work before a frame goes out on a
 device with no implicit sync

A DMA-BUF frame is handed to PipeWire after glFlush only, which leaves the ordering to implicit
sync. A GPU node that is not a DRM device (KGSL in an Android container: the Android backend's
and the virtual backend's named device) has none, so a consumer (the phone's floating window,
the presenter of a headless workspace) could read a frame the GPU had not finished; as with
Nvidia and llvmpipe, glFinish first there.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-02
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic: screencast on GPUs without implicit sync]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:workspace.headless
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/research/97
Origin: vendor
